WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:07.860
You mustn't call us cute!
kawaii nante sonna koto ittcha dame desu

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.910
Fluffy and lighthearted
fuwa fuwa

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:26.170
The strawberry girls are coming
ichigotachi ga yattekuru

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:30.510
Loud voices are coming closer
urusai koe ga chikazuite kuru

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.800
Fluffy and lighthearted
fuwa fuwa

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.970
The strawberry girls are coming
ichigo tachi ga yattekuru

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.520
They smell sweet and sour
amakute suppai kaori ga suru

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.770
It doesn't matter if the colors are mixed up
chiguhagu na iro de iimon

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.520
Let's draw some graffiti
rakugaki shichao

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.860
It's only natural that we'll make mistakes
shippai mo atarimae dayone

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.280
So you'd better forgive us!
watashitachi wo yurushite agenasai!

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.000
Don't get mad, don't get mad
okoranaidene, okoranaide

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.790
Just let us do what we want
suki ni sasete ne

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.500
Adults can't understand this
otona niwa wakaranai

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.840
Amazing! Miracle! Perfect!
suteki! kiseki! kanpeki!

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:16.590
You mustn't say we're cute!
kawaii nante sonna koto ittcha dame desu

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.260
Dazzling smiles
totetsumonai egao

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.720
Marshmallow-y sweet girls!
mashimaro na onnanoko

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.480
S-T-R-A-W-B-E-R-R-Y Girl!
I-C-H-I-G-O Girl!

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.480
Go, go, girl! "Strawberry" LOVE
Go, go, girl! "Ichigo" LOVE!

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.030
E-Excuse me? I'd like to try this.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.410
Yes.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:45.830
Oh. It didn't fit me. Smaller size, please.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.370
Yes.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.130
Oh, good!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:49.920
Yes.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.920
How much is this?

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:52.840
Yes.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.970
How much is this?

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.300
Yes.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.310
I'm asking you how much it is?

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.520
I couldn't hear you very clearly.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.480
Sorry.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.980
How much is this?

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.690
yen

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.690
"Two"... one thousand yen.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.870
O-Okay, I'll take it.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.660
Thank you.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.410
Y-You're getting a lot better.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.920
This place is no good!

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:29.870
Huh?

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.000
I can't get in the mood to speak English in a place that's so totally Japanese!

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.920
Well, this is Japan.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.180
From now on, let's do this at my house.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.930
Will you come to my house next Sunday?

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.810
Huh? Okay.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.980
Oh, but I promised Chika-chan I'd go to her house around noon next Sunday.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.440
How about after that?
Can you come at two?

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.530
Yes, that should be fine.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.950
It's decided then! Oh, and...

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.870
Please keep this a secret from
Onee-sama and the others!

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.660
O-Okay.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.500
And make sure you don't tell them that you're coming to my house.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.960
That will make it easier to practice, don't you think?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.800
Y-You're right. I understand.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:20.800
House Call

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.010
1776, Declaration of Independance...

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.930
This declaration was...

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.820
I don't know.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.530
It sure is spring.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.660
Miu
Receiving

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.170
Oh, it's only Miu.
Miu
Receiving

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.040
Hello!

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.840
<i>Hello.</i>

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.670
<i>Listen very carefully to what I'm about to say.</i>

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.890
<i>Right now, your precious Matsuri-chan is in my possession.</i>

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.220
<i>If you want to save her...</i>

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.930
<i>That'll be 5,000 yen, tax included!</i>

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.520
<i>Matsuri-chan, scream.</i>

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.390
<i>H-Huh?</i>

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.100
<i>Just scream and say, "It hurts."</i>

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.980
<i>It hurts.</i>

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.270
<i>Say, "I've been pinched."</i>

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.190
<i>I've been pinched!</i>

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:24.240
You know, I'm writing a report right now.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.820
It's due on Monday.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.740
<i>Hey!</i>

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.290
<i>Don't you care about Matsuri-chan?</i>

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.950
<i>I'll do worse things to her!</i>

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.960
Okay, okay, I'm coming.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.750
Oh well.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.340
I guess I'll play along a little bit.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.470
Matsuri-chan, are you okay?

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.470
Huh?

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.640
How good of you to come.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.730
Why are you the one that's tied up?

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.150
Rescue me!

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.660
Let's see... You said 5,000 yen, tax included, right?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.780
Okay, we're all done here.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.750
Wait, Onee-chan! Chi-chan, untie me!

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:17.500
What? But I'm playing the criminal.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.420
No "buts"! Just do it quickly!

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.130
I have to get going soon.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.220
What?

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.590
Where are you going?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.840
Well, at two, Ana...

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.430
Ana?

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.060
You made plans with Ana-chan?

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.970
No, never!

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:37.270
Um... Um... ana... ana... anago sushi roll!

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:44.110
Yes! We're going to make sea eel sushi, so Mom said I have to come home early.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.030
So, I'll go home now!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:45.860
Wait a minute!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.150
Huh?

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.320
If you go, there's no guarantee that I'll live!

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.290
Wh-What?!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.120
The ransom money is about 5 million yen!

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.830
When did the victim turn into the criminal?

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.500
I don't have that kind of money!

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.380
Uh, you don't need to take her seriously.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.380
Are you telling me you value money more than my life?

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.010
I can go home now, right?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.440
If you're determined to leave, then you might as well kill me now.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.150
Wh-What...?

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:23.610
This is becoming increasingly nonsensical.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:24.980
Onee-chan!

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.570
Wh-What should I do?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.460
I guess I could help you...

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.260
Um...

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.970
Okay, you can go now!

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.430
Thanks, Nobue-oneechan!

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.940
I didn't know you had a cat costume.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.230
I don't know anything about it.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.360
What?

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:05.860
Then...

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.240
Dirty old man.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.870
<b>School Zone</b>

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.380
I finally escaped.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.170
Yes, hello.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:33.680
<i>Matsuri-chan? What happened to you?
It's already past 2!</i>

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.010
I-I was late leaving Chika-chan's house.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.520
I'll be there soon.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.980
<i>I just want to be sure, you're alone, right?</i>

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.810
Yes, I'm by m-my...

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.400
<i>Hello? Matsuri-chan?</i>

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.730
I-I'll call you back.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.820
Miu-chan?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.410
Oh, hi, Matsuri-chan. What a coincidence.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.540
Coincidence?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.000
Matsuri-chan, I thought you went home?

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.000
Y-Yes, I'm just on my way now.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.080
Bye!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.630
Hey, since when is your house that way?

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:08.880
U-Um...

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.840
I was asked to do some shopping, so...

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.390
Well, let's all go together then.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:16.600
What?!

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:19.180
Yeah, we were on our way to your house anyway.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.980
Oh no, that won't do!

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.190
Then give me 5 million yen.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.570
Huh?!

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.690
Um...

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.610
Oh! She ran away!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.410
Oh, she fell.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.330
Matsuri-chan, are you okay?

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.660
W-What should I do?

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.290
Um...

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.000
Look! It's a flying saucer!

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:54.260
H-Huh? Aren't you gonna look?

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.970
More importantly, Matsuri-chan, behind you...

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.560
...I can see a ghost!

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.510
What?!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.310
But he sure isn't very lively.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.270
Well, that's 'cause he's a ghost.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.730
I'm going to try and talk to him.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.740
It's no good. He's Italian.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.360
R-Really?

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.700
How far are you gonna take this?

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.540
Onee-chan, what would someone have to say to make you turn around?

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.660
Hm, let me see...

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:27.580
If you say "nya" at the end of your sentence, or...

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.590
Nya?

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:31.710
Nya...

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:41.930
Hello, nya.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.560
No, a little more like this.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.350
Huh? Oh...

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.810
Hello, nya!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.030
Huh? Weren't you facing the other way?

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.540
We were, but...

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:03.660
Matsuri-chan, your sentence-ending!

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.040
Oh no, that's a problem, nya!

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.880
Hello, nya.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.550
<i>What happened? Is something wrong?</i>

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.010
I'm sorry, nya.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.010
I'll be right there for sure, nya.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:18.800
<i>Nya?</i>

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.390
Okay, I'm hanging up, nya.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.810
I must go home alone today, nya.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.600
So you can't follow me, nya.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.520
Do you understand, nya?

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.060
D-Do you understand, nya?

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.860
I understand, nya.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:34.820
Dirty old man.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:35.730
<i>Recycling...</i>

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.700
Well, we can't inconvenience Matsuri-chan.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.410
Why don't we go to Ana-chan's house?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.530
Yeah.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.660
Huh? Um... But...

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.120
Bye!
But that's...

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.210
Get home safely.
...that's a problem, nya.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.840
Is this it?

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.220
It's huge!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.180
You probably shouldn't...

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.720
Shoot. She's rich!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.310
It looks fancy!

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.890
What a show off!

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.520
This is the kind of house where you ring the doorbell and run away!

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.110
Yes, coming!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:19.200
That sure took you awhile!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.070
Uh...

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:25.830
Hello.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.870
I know it's sudden, but we came over.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:31.210
I-I'm sorry.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.080
O-Oh, I-I see.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.460
P-Please come in.

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.000
Thanks for your hospitality!

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:38.710
What an amazing house!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.420
Oh, it's not much, really.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.380
Hey, no fair!

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.480
P-Please, come in.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:01.200
So, this is your room.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.240
It's such a cute room!

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.240
Oh, no, you're too kind.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.950
It really does seem like a genuine foreigner's room.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.370
You have a computer, too!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.250
What do you use it for?

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.090
Um, for drawing pictures and...

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.920
Note: Let's Learn Together! Beginner's English

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.050
Is something wrong?

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:27.550
Oh, it's nothing.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:34.900
This is why I told you not to bring them here!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.310
I'm sorry.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:39.480
You absolutely can't tell them you came here to practice English with me.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:40.480
O-Okay.

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:43.280
By the way, where'd Miu go?

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.240
We forgot all about her.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.370
Oh my!

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.280
Miu-san is here as well?

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.700
She's supposed to be, but...

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.540
Where did she wander off to?

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:55.830
Don't fall asleep!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:56.880
Live!

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:58.420
Don't underestimate the mountain!

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.970
They think they're so great, building a wall like this!

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.100
Help me!

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.480
Did she sneak into the yard?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.360
Ana-chan, whose dog is that?

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.490
Um... His name is Frusciante.
He's our pet.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.580
I guess we have to help her.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:30.580
He doesn't bite, does he?

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.870
I don't think so.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.120
Get away!

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.340
Hey, who's chasing who?

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.340
That would be you.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:44.010
Don't just watch! Do something!

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:47.720
Come on, stop it, Fruanshite!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.800
No, it's Frusciante!

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.720
Oh, okay.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.600
Frushiaten!!

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.560
You're getting it wrong on purpose!

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.480
Can I bring you something?

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:03.820
Yes, please.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.150
Anyhow, what's wrong with your dog?!

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.820
He's so poorly trained!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.530
It's your fault for sneaking in the yard.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:15.790
Actually, as a guard dog, he's trained well.
He should be praised.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.160
Right?

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.540
Anyhow, isn't his name way too long?

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:23.750
That's it!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.090
From today, your name will be Fu-chan!

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.340
Huh?

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.840
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:29.800
Huh?

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:32.680
Note: Fu-chan

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:37.140
Shikoku?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.140
Isn't this Gifuhashima?

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.560
That's a train station.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:44.190
I think it's England, nya!

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:44.900
Nya?

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.860
Hey, Ana-chan, whereabouts was your home?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.700
It was on a peninsula in the southwest, a place called Cornwall.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.740
It's the warmest place in England.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:00.870
It's surrounded by lots of nature, and it's so very, very beautiful!

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.040
Nature...

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.380
Lots...

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:07.630
Cornwall.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.630
Corn...

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.300
Half-price.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.850
So, just what are you trying to say?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:18.560
What?

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.480
Hey, Primal and Red Hot Chili Peppers!

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.940
It's all western music CD's.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.860
I guess that's to be expected.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:29.450
Do you know them, Onee-sama?

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.320
Sure, I listen to them quite a bit.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.370
I'm so glad.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.950
Nobody around here knows them.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.620
Well, there aren't many elementary school kids...

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.540
...who listen to western music.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:46.460
It's so wonderful that there's someone like you near by.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.760
I don't have many conversation topics in common with children my age...

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:54.260
Yes, well, they say Japanese kids are immature compared to westerners.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.010
Hey, I know Primal!

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:59.140
They were in last year's
Red and White Song Festival!

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.640
I said this was western music!

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.480
Weren't they on the red team?

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:07.110
Oh yeah! Which CDs do you listen to a lot?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.690
Um... What...

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:14.780
Um... Which...
Would you like to come to my room?

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.700
I keep my favorites there!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.160
Yeah, let's go.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.670
What happened to the tea?

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.090
Oh, you have this one.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.220
If you'd like, you can borrow it.

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.470
Really?

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.800
Of course!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:37.930
Onee-chan!

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:39.680
What?

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:42.520
I found "The Three Manju Brothers"!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.150
An international version?

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:46.690
No, no! You've got it all wrong!

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.650
Father got that from his work!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.490
But there's a name on the back.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.530
<b>Ana's</b>

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:02.870
And I found "Fish Store Heaven," too!

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:06.630
There's nothing strange about that.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.000
She is an elementary school student.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.460
N-No, Onee-sama!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:12.710
I, um, got those when I was in kindergarten.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.970
Did "The Three Manju Brothers" come out that long ago?

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:22.980
Anyhow, it's unbelievably rude of you to just go through someone's shelves.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:24.480
Please, stop it.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.520
Fine, then...

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.150
Ana Coppola.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.110
It's earned a flower circle.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.660
Don't tape things to the wall without asking.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:38.240
But it's flower circle-quality work.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.700
Awful things happened to me at my last school because of my name.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.040
So please, stop it!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.960
There's no need for you to be so negative about your name.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.000
Onee-sama...

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.380
Your parents gave you that name.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.970
You should take more pride in it.

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:58.220
But you can't deny that it's a weird name.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.600
But is it really such a weird name?

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:03.310
Onee-sama...

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.980
There's a famous movie director with the last name Coppola, too.

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.810
An amazing person has the same name as you!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.770
But if a Japanese person heard it, they'd immediately laugh.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:16.950
It's not the name that matters, it's what's inside that's important.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:17.990
Onee-sama...

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.490
If you have confidence in yourself...

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.660
...I don't think anyone will pay attention to your name.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.750
But in reality, your name alone can decide your character and role...

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:31.750
...and basically, your whole life can be decided by your name.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:38.130
Don't worry, if we shut her up, no one will know at school.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.390
What?

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.300
I was just telling the truth!

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:46.180
If you keep saying that,
I'll give you a weird name!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.680
Like what? Like what?

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.100
Kondosare Shibamata.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:51.310
Why?

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:53.860
Just go, Kondosare Shibamata!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.650
Hey! You're always taking Ana-chan's side!

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:58.610
Fine...

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:00.570
I'll win this by showing how flexible I am!

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.370
Huh?

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:03.620
Take a look at this!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.660
See! Isn't it amazing?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.460
What the heck is up with that?

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.830
That's not amazing so much as too flexible.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:14.750
Well, at school, they call me "Hiroshou's gazelle."

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.420
That's a name you give to a fast runner.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.340
We drank the tea.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:24.260
What great timing!
Matsuri-chan, come here.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.760
Huh? Me?

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.430
Just sit down.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.810
Huh?

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.480
Here we go. Ready and...

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:36.270
Matsuri-chan, you're not very flexible for a cat.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.440
No, it's more that you're just overly flexible.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.780
Onee-chan, what are you guys doing?

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:43.280
Okay, Chi-chan, you're next!

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:47.080
I don't have a flexible body either!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.160
I'm fine as I am, so what does it matter?

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:50.960
What are you saying?

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.750
You can benefit a lot from being flexible!

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:56.590
For example, when you drop your eraser...

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:00.720
If you're flexible...

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.390
...you can pick it up, like so!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.050
Or squat.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:06.560
Okay, Coppola-chan...

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:12.350
Hey.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:14.480
Why us, too?

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.480
Never mind, just stay outside.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:18.230
Oh well.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.190
Let's look around the house.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.330
There are so many clothes!

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:41.090
There're just so many!

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.770
Can you hit my back a little?

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:53.140
Huh?

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.230
Hitting won't make them pop out.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.570
Hey, girls. We're gonna get going pretty soon.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.490
Already?

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.570
I'm sorry, Ana-chan.

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.370
She's an idiot, but please forgive her.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.410
Uh-huh.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.580
Huh?

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:25.430
Um... Uh... That's...

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:30.310
Let me guess, Ana-chan... Are you teaching your friend English?

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:36.850
Yes! But it's been quite difficult to teach someone a language.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:40.230
Cool! Teach me too!

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:41.820
Let me see...

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:44.780
Oh! Very pretty!

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.910
How much is this?

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:59.210
"T-Two"... one thousand yen.

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:09.970
Y-You've really improved, nya!

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:26.030
When I remembered my forgotten dream
wasurekaketa yume wo omoidashitara

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:37.290
Suddenly your smile came to mind
fui ni kimi no egao ga ukandekitayo

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:43.840
Without even thinking about tomorrow
ashita sae mada shiranai

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:49.260
We used to play all day
nee asonde bakari ita ano hi

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:55.180
Even when there was a steep downhill
kyuuna sakamichi demo

00:22:55.180 --> 00:23:03.400
We ran as we pretended to have no fear
nee heiki na furi shite hashitta

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:07.030
Hurry! Hurry!
isoide isoide

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:14.740
A naughty shadow whispers in your ear
mimimoto de sasayaku itazura kageboshi

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.410
Our skirts fluttered
sukaato yurameki

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:23.460
As a cool breeze tapped our knees
suzukaze ga hiza wo tataita

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:34.680
Where are you right now?
anone kimi wa ima doko ni imasuka?

00:23:41.480 --> 00:23:42.770
I-It's terrible news!

00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:46.570
I just saw something frilly and fluttery at the restaurant with my very own eyes!

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:47.900
Calm down, Ana-chan.

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:49.530
What exactly did you see?

00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:50.860
This, this, that and the other...

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:53.950
What? Onee-chan has a part-time job?

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:55.830
Oh no, Micchan, when did you get here?

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:58.500
Let's go check it out, right away!
Let's go!

00:23:58.500 --> 00:23:59.540
Hey, wait!

00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:02.870
Oh no, have I let loose a terrible vicious beast?

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:04.420
Maybe so.

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:09.300
Watch the next "Marshmallow"!
Part-time Job
Next

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:10.050
Part-time Job
Next
